 ## Overview
-Cinematic Quality Volumetric Clouds is a high-fidelity rendering technique that generates volumetric clouds by ray marching through a 3D Perlin noise field and applying Beer's law for light absorption [S1, unofficial][S2]. It solves the problem of visual fidelity in cloud rendering by bypassing the resolution and optimization constraints of real-time approximations in favor of per-pixel ray tracing [S2]. Unlike its siblings, which prioritize frame rate through spatial discretization or precomputation, this method achieves cinematic quality by enabling high-quality aerial perspective, per-sample atmospheric transmittance, and multi-scattering approximations, at the cost of significant performance overhead [S2].
